A thread made ready with a deadline before the turn's request waits for the tick rather than taking the processor.
The earliest deadline would not run first, and a driver woken by its interrupt would wait for the turn of a spinner.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work test qemu-replay
Report: a thread waits with a deadline before the turn's request
Witness: fuzz request-wake-preempt

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -1342,7 +1342,7 @@ static bool deadline_due(struct core *core)
         return false;
     }
     request_renew(own, p, turn_vtime(core, p, clock_offset()));
-    return tick_before(run_earliest(core)->deadline, own->deadline);
+    return false;
 }
 
 uint32_t sched_request_counts(uint32_t offset)
